  title: "Two Oceans, One Passage: The Arctic Searches, 1576-1909",
  description: "How three centuries of searchers approached the Northwest Passage from the Atlantic and the Pacific, how the Franklin search of 1848-1859 mapped the archipelago, how Inuit knowledge made the expeditions possible and finally explained their end, and how the searches became Canada's claim to the Arctic.",
